# Allowlist, not a denylist: same rationale as claude/.gitignore.
#
# ~/.config/herdr is tree-folded into this directory, so everything herdr writes
# at runtime lands here. Each release adds more (sockets, session.json,
# session-snapshots/, logs, the plugin lock), so enumerating them loses.
# Ignore the lot, re-include only the configuration.
.config/herdr/*
!.config/herdr/config.toml
